because I can talk about that for a second.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:23.040
That was something I expected to be an improvement

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.300
over the first Metal Gear

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:27.560
and am disappointed to find out that they didn't fix that.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.080
What a pain in the butt

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:32.640
that the key card for key card one

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.280
opens up doors beyond the moment

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.000
that you collect key card two.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:41.440
But key card two isn't key card one plus two.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.840
It only opens doors that are key card two.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.440
So you have to know which card to use.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.640
Of course, that would be great

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:50.140
if the doors were labeled for them.

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:52.060
So instead, you just go up to a door

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:53.760
and it doesn't open when you have key card two.

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:55.540
So you're like, all right, I guess I'll try key card one,

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.600
which doesn't sound like too big of a deal, right?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:58.560
What's Mike complaining about?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.140
You got to just move through the menus and everything.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:01.180
There's eight of them.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:02.960
Eight key cards that you got to get through.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.980
And you got to be like, all right, wait, is it this one?

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.600
Because key cards three, four, five, six,

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.140
they're all still showing up.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:12.940
It is the video game equivalent of going,

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:17.940
of that classic sight gag of somebody going through each key

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:19.780
on a key ring one by one.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:23.380
And all they needed to do was color code them.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.120
Put something next to the door on the actual field of play

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:32.840
that was colored the same as the key card in your inventory.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.340
And it would have been fine.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.780
But no, they just didn't do that.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:37.960
And it made it goofy.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:42.300
Yeah, and I do think that even if they did do that,

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:45.620
the going to the menu to get the key card every time

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:49.120
does feel like it doesn't add anything to my gameplay.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.400
You know, I get it.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.720
Like, that's what you'd have to do.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.800
You'd have to pick up the key card and put it in the door every time.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:58.620
But like, I thought when I was in that first building

00:18:58.620 --> 00:18:59.800
and I got key card one,

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.500
apparently picking up key card one auto selects it.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:06.040
So maybe that was the only gadget I had or whatever,

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.440
a piece of equipment or whatever it is

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.340
that I had.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.500
So it was just automatically selected.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.400
